@startuml
title Invoice Workflow — Component View
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Application users" as Users
component "Browser UI" as Browser <<presentation>>

node "One FastAPI application" {
  component "HTTP boundary" as HTTP <<presentation>>
  component "Definition / invoice / approval\napplication services" as Services <<application>>
  component "Execution coordinator" as Coordinator <<application>>
  component "Orchestration strategy" as Orchestration <<application>>
  component "Choreography strategy" as Choreography <<application>>
  component "Definition validator" as Validator <<domain>>
  component "Shared step service\nretry policy + resolver" as Step <<domain>>
  component "Closed executor registry" as Executors <<application>>
  component "Run-scoped EventBus" as EventBus <<infrastructure>>
  component "Repositories / unit of work" as Repositories <<infrastructure>>
  component "PDF + document adapters" as Documents <<infrastructure>>
  component "Deterministic archive scenario adapter" as Faults <<application adapter>>
}

database "Persistent database" as Database
folder "Controlled document storage" as Storage
component "Selected PDF library" as PdfLib <<third-party library>>

Users --> Browser
Browser --> HTTP
HTTP --> Services
Services --> Validator
Services --> Coordinator
Coordinator --> Orchestration
Coordinator --> Choreography
Orchestration --> Step
Choreography --> Step
Choreography --> EventBus
Step --> Executors
Executors --> Documents
Executors --> Faults
Services --> Repositories
Coordinator --> Repositories
Step --> Repositories
Repositories --> Database
Documents --> Storage
Documents --> PdfLib

note right of EventBus
Transient trigger only.
One handler for one active run scope.
No subscriber while waiting.
end note

note bottom of Step
Business failure is not retried.
Only retryable technical failure
below the bound repeats the task.
end note

legend
Dependencies point toward shared policy.
No broker, external workflow engine, OCR, or business service.
Final conceptual components; API paths and class names are omitted for clarity.
endlegend
@enduml
